  "body": "**A plasma profile operation: a 2D through-cut with kerf, leads, cut direction and small-hole rules.**\n\n- **Geometry:** closed or open 2D contours, inner and outer, cut through with no depth stepping.\n- **Kerf:** the torch's kerf width, applied in the computer (offset path). An option posts G41/G42 instead, with PathPilot's rule of a straight G1 entry longer than the tool radius ([Tormach post guidelines](https://knowledgebase.tormach.com/8l/pathpilot-post-processor-guidelines)).\n- **Direction:** outside contours CW, inside CCW (Hypertherm: the square edge on the part). It's overridable, and the override is stated.\n- **Leads:** an arc lead-in and lead-out by default, with lengths as parameters.\n  - **Small holes:** for Ø below a threshold (default 32 mm, or under 1.5× thickness), use a perpendicular lead-in from near the centre (≤ the radius), **no lead-out**, an optional overburn, and a 60–70 % feed factor (LinuxCNC Plasma Primer §13). A 1300PL forum report links hole lead-outs to arc loss.\n- **Cut order:** inner contours before their outer contour, so a part never drops before its holes are cut.\n- **Parameters:** feed is optional, since M200 (AutoFS) sets it on the 1300PL. Pierce height, cut height and delay are optional; when left blank, the controller's AutoFS decides.\n\n**Done means:**\n- the op generates offset XY paths with leads in the stated directions, inner first;\n- small holes take the hole rule;\n- it's undoable through commands and round-trips through the project file;\n- golden CL output is pinned for a plate with holes.\n\nPart of #621\n",
